hdClaude @VERSION@ for Houdini @HOUDINI_VERSION@ (Windows x64)
=====================================================

hdClaude is a spectral GPU path tracer for Solaris, written as an OpenUSD
Hydra render delegate. It renders through Vulkan ray queries and shades
MaterialX materials (standard_surface, open_pbr_surface, UsdPreviewSurface).

Source, documentation and issues:
  https://github.com/paoloemilioselva/hdClaude


Requirements
------------

- Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.

- Houdini @HOUDINI_VERSION@, installed at its default location:

    @HOUDINI_ROOT@

  Download it from https://www.sidefx.com/download/ (choose the exact build
  @HOUDINI_VERSION@, under "All builds" if it is no longer the current one).
  The plugin reads Houdini's MaterialX libraries from that directory. With a
  different build, or Houdini installed elsewhere, the plugin loads but no
  material compiles.

- A GPU and driver with Vulkan 1.3 and these extensions:
    VK_KHR_ray_query
    VK_KHR_acceleration_structure
    VK_KHR_buffer_device_address
    VK_KHR_deferred_host_operations
    descriptor indexing
  The Vulkan runtime comes with the GPU driver; no Vulkan SDK is needed.
  Use a current driver from your GPU vendor. Developed and tested on an
  NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti.


Install
-------

1. Close Houdini.

2. Extract this zip into your Houdini user preferences directory, the
   houdini22.0 folder in your Documents:

     %USERPROFILE%\Documents\houdini22.0

   If OneDrive manages your Documents folder, it is instead:

     %USERPROFILE%\OneDrive\Documents\houdini22.0

   If you set HOUDINI_USER_PREF_DIR, it is that directory.

   Afterwards that directory contains:

     hdClaude\                  the plugin
     packages\hdClaude.json     the package that tells Houdini to load it

   The package finds the plugin as $HOUDINI_USER_PREF_DIR/hdClaude, so both
   must be in the same preferences directory.

3. Start Houdini. In a Solaris viewport, choose "Claude GPU Path Tracer" from
   the renderer menu.

To check the package was found, run this from a Houdini command line:

    hconfig -ap

HOUDINI_PATH should list the hdClaude directory, and HDCLAUDE_DEPTH_STYLE
should be "linear".


Settings
--------

The viewport's Display Options and the Render Settings LOP show hdClaude's
settings. Each is also an HDCLAUDE_* environment variable; see
docs/building.md in the repository.

Compiled shaders are cached on disk, so the first render of a new material
takes longer than the ones after it.


Uninstall
---------

Delete hdClaude\ and packages\hdClaude.json from the preferences directory.


Licence
-------

hdClaude is MIT licensed; see hdClaude\licenses\hdClaude.txt. It includes
glslang, volk, the Vulkan Memory Allocator and the Vulkan headers, whose
licences are in the same directory.
